# Files that are read by Linux containers must be checked out with LF, even on
# Windows. Without this, git's autocrlf turns db-init.sh into CRLF on checkout,
# the file is bind-mounted into the SQL Server container as-is, and bash reads
# `set -euo pipefail\r` - reporting `set: pipefail: invalid option name`, where
# the trailing \r is invisible in the error. The same class of failure has also
# appeared on the VM as `$'\r': command not found`.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
